cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this manuscript, please cite the preferred citation below."
title: "Critical Jumps for Rough Polynomial Carleson Operators with Angular Hardy Data and Finite Radial Variation"
authors:
  - family-names: "Tseng"
version: "4.1"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
url: "https://github.com/Tseng-math/rough-polynomial-fluctuation-theory"
abstract: >-
  Strong Lp critical-jump bounds hold for every 1 < p < infinity and
  mean-zero angular Hardy H1 data on the sphere, with the bounded-degree
  polynomial phase supremum and jump-amplitude supremum both inside the
  spatial norm. For each fixed polynomial phase, mean-zero angular L log L
  data give a weak type (1,1) estimate uniform in the polynomial coefficients.
  Both estimates allow each fixed radial amplitude of finite rho-variation,
  1 <= rho < infinity, and concern complete sharp-truncation trajectories.
  They imply maximal-truncation bounds, r-variation for r > 2, and
  principal-value convergence.
